# Exposure (K5, DESIGN.md §10.4). Revealing a secret membership is news like an act. When a
# faction learns that one of its members is secretly in a faction it's at war with, its
# exposed table decides: keep (and a conflict opens), demote, or expel. Riverhold's keeps a
# member with standing 60 or more at −30, and otherwise expels at −40.

load content/sample

# The player becomes a double agent: openly in the Free Company, with Ava, and secretly in
# the Lantern Guild, which then goes to war with the Company. No conflict opens: the
# Company doesn't know.
act player steal --scale 4
join player free_company
join merchant_ava free_company
join player lantern_guild --secretly
relate lantern_guild free_company -60

# Ava sees through it, and the Company learns through her. The player's standing with the
# Company is 0, so it expels them at −40, which spills +2.40 to the Guild (−60: −0.06).
expose player lantern_guild --seen-by merchant_ava --explain
assert standing player free_company == -40.00
assert standing player lantern_guild == 2.40
assert show character player == player — The Player — law -20.00, good -12.00 — True Neutral — member of lantern_guild (cutpurse, secretly) since tick 0

# The news goes on from Ava to Hale and Mira, ten ticks later; neither is in a faction at
# war with the Guild that the player belongs to, so they only learn.
advance 10
news

# Revealed to everyone, the membership is open.
expose player lantern_guild
assert show character player == player — The Player — law -20.00, good -12.00 — True Neutral — member of lantern_guild (cutpurse) since tick 0
